Apple's eighth-generation <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad-mini/">iPad mini</a> went on sale <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/06/ipad-mini-oled-and-m6-imac-available-today/">earlier this month</a> with a larger <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> display, a thinner and lighter design, the A20 Pro chip, and water and dust resistance. If you still use the sixth-generation &zwnj;iPad mini&zwnj; from 2021, the upgrade also brings changes that <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ipad-mini-6-vs-7/">debuted on the 2024 model</a>, including <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-pencil/">Apple Pencil</a> Pro support, and twice the USB-C transfer speed.<br/>
